#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:52
msgid "Drain System for a Tank"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:53
msgid "While the ‘tank with a valve’ scenario is not a good constant head solution, we can use our understanding of the system to properly design drain systems for AguaClara reactors like flocculators and clarifiers, since they are just tanks with valves. The derivation for the following equation is here, along with more details on AguaClara’s pipe stub method for draining tanks: :ref:`heading_diameter_and_time_tank_drain_equation`. The derived ‘Tank Drain’ equation is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:55
msgid "D_{Pipe} = \\sqrt{ \\frac{8 L_{Tank} W_{Tank}}{\\pi t_{Drain}}} {\\left( \\frac{H_{Tank} \\sum K }{2g} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:59
msgid "The equation can also be rearranged to solve for the time it would take to drain a tank given its dimensions and a certain drain pipe size:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:61
msgid "t_{Drain} =  \\frac{8 L_{Tank} W_{Tank}}{\\pi D_{Pipe}^2} {\\left( \\frac{H_{Tank} \\sum K }{2g} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:65
msgid "Such that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:66
msgid ":math:`D_{Pipe}` = Diameter of the drain piping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:67
msgid ":math:`L_{Tank}, W_{Tank}, H_{Tank}` = Tank dimensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:68
msgid ":math:`t_{Drain}` = Time it takes to drain the tank"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flow_Control_and_Measurement/FCM_Intro.rst:69
msgid ":math:`\\sum K` = Sum of all the minor loss coefficients in the system"
msgstr ""

